HCG 5000 IU – Research and Scientific Overview

What Is HCG?

Human Chorionic Gonadotropin (HCG) is a glycoprotein hormone studied for its role in reproductive biology, endocrine function, and hormonal signaling.

HCG interacts with luteinizing hormone (LH) receptors, making it an important subject in reproductive and endocrine research.

